    {
      "id": "cymbeline/sceneIII_7.1/p@82648",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "QUEEN.\nAnd, to kill the marvel,\nShall be so ever.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "cymbeline/sceneIII_7.1/p@82648/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 6,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "cymbeline/sceneIII_7.1/p@82648/line-2",
          "start": 7,
          "end": 31,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "cymbeline/sceneIII_7.1/p@82648/line-3",
          "start": 32,
          "end": 49,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 1131487,
        "end": 1131571,
        "line": 43048,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap07/p@82648",
        "anchor": "sceneIII_7.1"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "QUEEN.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 6
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "cymbeline/sceneIII_7.1/p@82736",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "CLOTEN.\nThere be many Cæsars ere such another Julius. Britain is a world by itself, and we will nothing pay for wearing our own noses.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "cymbeline/sceneIII_7.1/p@82736/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 7,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "cymbeline/sceneIII_7.1/p@82736/line-2",
          "start": 8,
          "end": 134,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 1131575,
        "end": 1131740,
        "line": 43054,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap07/p@82736",
        "anchor": "sceneIII_7.1"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "CLOTEN.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "cymbeline/sceneIII_7.1/p@82905",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "QUEEN.\nThat opportunity,\nWhich then they had to take from’s, to resume\nWe have again. Remember, sir, my liege,\nThe kings your ancestors, together with\nThe natural bravery of your isle, which stands\nAs Neptune’s park, ribb’d and pal’d in\nWith rocks unscaleable and roaring waters,\nWith sands that will not bear your enemies’ boats\nBut suck them up to th’ top-mast. A kind of conquest\nCæsar made here, but made not here his brag\nOf ‘Came, and saw, and overcame.’ With shame\n(The first that ever touch’d him) he was carried\nFrom off our coast, twice beaten; and his shipping\n(Poor ignorant baubles!) on our terrible seas,\nLike egg-shells mov’d upon their surges, crack’d\nAs easily ’gainst our rocks; for joy whereof\nThe fam’d Cassibelan, who was once at point\n(O, giglot fortune!) to master Cæsar’s sword,\nMade Lud’s Town with rejoicing fires bright\nAnd Britons strut with courage.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
